-- title:
--   Transport of the universal-family package along a variable change
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq 2$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and $E_0$ a Weierstrass curve over $k$ with invertible discriminant (elliptic). Let $W_0$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $C_0$ be a variable change over $k$, and let $\mathcal{E}$ be a Weierstrass curve over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ whose discriminant $\Delta$ is a unit, such that the reduction of $\mathcal{E}$ along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ (t \mapsto 0)$ equals $C_0 \cdot E_0$. Assume that the Hasse invariant of $\mathcal{E}$ reduced coefficientwise to $k\llbracket t\rrbracket$ — the coefficient of degree $q-1$ in the $((q-1)/2)$-th power of the two-torsion polynomial — has vanishing constant term and nonvanishing $t$-coefficient, and that $j(\mathcal{E}) - a_0 = u_2 t^{e}$ for some $a_0 \in W_0$, some $e \geq 1$ and some unit $u_2$ of $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ (here $j(\mathcal{E})$ is the $j$-invariant formed from the invertibility of $\Delta$). The conclusion asserts the existence of: a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal{E}'$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ with unit discriminant whose reduction along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ (t \mapsto 0)$ is $E_0$ itself; a commutative formal group $F$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ whose underlying two-variable power series is the fixed formal group law $\mathcal{E}'.\mathtt{formalGroupLawFixed}$ of $\mathcal{E}'$ and whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ (t \mapsto 0)$ is the formal group of $E_0$, i.e. the law of $E_0.\mathtt{formalGroup}$ is the coefficientwise image of that of $F$; such that, writing $[q] = F.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,q$ for the $q$-fold iterate built by substituting $([q-1], X)$ into the group law, the $t$-coefficient of the coefficient of $Z^{q}$ in $[q]$ is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$, and that coefficient of $Z^q$ equals $u_1 t$ modulo the ideal generated by $q$ for some unit $u_1$ of $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$; and finally $a_0 \in W_0$, $e \geq 1$ and a unit $u_2$ with $j(\mathcal{E}') - a_0 = u_2 t^{e}$.
--
--   This is the variable-change-equivariant form of the universal-deformation package attached to an ordinary-at-level-one situation: it allows the input deformation $\mathcal{E}$ to reduce only to some $k$-isomorphic model $C_0 \cdot E_0$ of $E_0$, while the output is the package for $E_0$ itself. It is used by the three constructions of such deformations according to whether $j(E_0)$ is $0$, $1728$, or neither.
